+ * because browsers carry their own trust store, but this app does not.
+ *
+ * The fix is deliberately narrow. [systemTrustManager] answers first and is the only thing that can
+ * say yes to everything the app already trusted, so nothing about the rest of the app changes;
+ * [isrgRootX2TrustManager] is consulted only when the platform rejects a chain. Both stay pinned to
+ * the WebDAV client - the Nightscout, CGM and Drive connections keep using the untouched default.
+ *
+ * Trust is not weakened: ISRG Root X2 is a public root run by the same organisation as the
+ * certificate authorities Android already trusts, host name verification still happens in OkHttp,
+ * and no certificate is accepted without a valid chain to that root.
